WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.478
Josh and Anne are gearing up for another adventure in the great outdoors.

2
00:00:04.479 --> 00:00:10.759
For this trip, they will spend two weeks backpacking through New Zealand, which sounds like fun, don't you think?

3
00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:17.133
However, this adventure will require getting some special gear before they head out.

4
00:00:17.134 --> 00:00:22.305
Anne and Josh decide to visit a store that sells a lot of backpacking supplies.

5
00:00:22.306 --> 00:00:28.980
Anne knows that the most important piece of equipment for when she's about to do a lot of hiking, is strong boots.

6
00:00:28.981 --> 00:00:37.738
She tries out a number of boots, walking up and down plastic mountains in the store to test how well they hold the ground.

7
00:00:37.739 --> 00:00:45.293
It looks like she has found some boots that are very light, waterproof, strong, and her favorite color─yellow!

8
00:00:45.294 --> 00:00:49.738
Josh, meanwhile, knows that the next most important purchase is poles.

9
00:00:49.739 --> 00:00:57.404
Scientists have recently discovered that walking downhill with a lot of weight is difficult for the knees to handle.

10
00:00:57.405 --> 00:01:05.915
In fact, a lot of people injure their knees by slipping downhill, but poles help the knees by providing extra support and balance.

11
00:01:05.916 --> 00:01:13.229
So Josh chooses some poles that are lightweight but strong enough to support his weight and grip the ground.

12
00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:19.917
The last big purchase is a backpack. Backpacks come in all colors, sizes, and weights.

13
00:01:19.918 --> 00:01:27.392
Bags that hold over seven kilograms have a padded strap that goes around the waist to help lift the weight off the shoulders.

14
00:01:27.393 --> 00:01:36.068
Josh picks a brown pack that will help him hide in the trees, and Anne picks a pack with her favorite color─yellow!

15
00:01:36.069 --> 00:01:40.629
There are a lot more pieces of equipment that Josh and Anne will need to go on their trip,

16
00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:48.223
such as headlamps, sleeping bags, a cookstove, food, hiking clothes, a first aid kit, and bug repellant.

17
00:01:48.224 --> 00:01:54.021
However, all of this can get expensive, so they borrow a lot of these things from their friends.

18
00:01:54.022 --> 00:02:00.436
"In order to stay safe when you go backpacking, it's important to have good gear," Josh says.

19
00:02:00.437 --> 00:02:03.982
Their bags are packed, and they are on their way to New Zealand!

20
00:02:03.983 --> 00:02:08.106
New Zealand is a beautiful country with many kinds of landscapes.

21
00:02:08.107 --> 00:02:15.107
There are beaches, forests, jungles, plains, mountains, and volcanoes, just to name a few.

22
00:02:15.108 --> 00:02:19.631
The country is about the same size as Korea, just a tiny bit bigger.

23
00:02:19.632 --> 00:02:24.600
But there are seventy million people living in Korea and only four million living in New Zealand.

24
00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:30.347
Of course, you can change the total to four million and two, now that Josh and Anne have landed!

25
00:02:30.348 --> 00:02:36.273
There are countless trails and hikes to choose from when you visit this beautiful country.

26
00:02:36.274 --> 00:02:43.689
Josh and Anne decide to try the most famous trail in New Zealand, which is nicknamed the Most Beautiful Walk in the World.

27
00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:46.146
It is a trail called the Milford Track.

28
00:02:46.147 --> 00:02:51.339
It will take four days to hike the 53 kilometers from one side of the mountain to the other.

29
00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:58.709
And because so many people like to visit Milford, they will sleep in huts instead of tents because it is easier on the wildlife.

30
00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:02.143
Josh and Anne arrive at Milford on a very sunny day.

31
00:03:02.144 --> 00:03:09.439
After walking a few kilometers, they pass by a river that is a color of blue Anne has never seen in a river before.

32
00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:13.827
She is tempted to dive in, but it is too cold!

33
00:03:13.828 --> 00:03:16.723
Later on in the hike, Josh meets a kea.

34
00:03:16.724 --> 00:03:20.795
Don't be fooled, this is a very smart and talented bird.

35
00:03:20.796 --> 00:03:25.545
While people aren't looking, it will unzip their backpacks and steal their lunches.

36
00:03:25.546 --> 00:03:31.968
Josh gets close enough to take a picture and leaves the disappointed kea waiting for its next victim.

37
00:03:31.969 --> 00:03:34.691
At the top of the mountain is Mackinnon Pass.

38
00:03:34.692 --> 00:03:38.117
The view is breathtaking, and so is the freezing wind!

39
00:03:38.118 --> 00:03:43.530
As they walk down the other side of the mountain, Josh and Anne are glad they have their poles.

40
00:03:43.531 --> 00:03:47.239
Along the way they find a powerful waterfall.

41
00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:52.433
Anne decides to test how waterproof her jacket is and steps underneath the falls.

42
00:03:52.434 --> 00:03:59.560
"It felt like a massage!" she says, emerging from the waterfall dry and smiling.

43
00:03:59.561 --> 00:04:06.257
The four days of hiking go by faster than they expected, and soon Josh and Anne are at the end of the trail.

44
00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:09.732
"What did you think of Milford?" Anne asked.

45
00:04:09.733 --> 00:04:14.719
"It's so beautiful, my feet aren't even tired!" said Josh.

46
00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:19.876
"I agree. I can't wait to come back and do it again!" said Anne.

47
00:04:19.877 --> 00:04:22.120
The first trail was a success.

48
00:04:22.121 --> 00:04:29.436
With another 12 days to go, Josh and Anne are thankful they have such great gear and such a beautiful country to visit.

